        <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of epidermoid head and neck cancer with cisplatinum/bleomycin vs methotrexate/vindesine].</ArticleTitle>
        <Pagination>
          <MedlinePgn>331-3</MedlinePgn>
        </Pagination>
        <Abstract>
          <AbstractText>Treatment of patients with advanced squamous head and neck tumors demonstrates even with best surgical and x-ray techniques only five year survival rats between 10 and 30%. Chemotherapy in addition seems to improve these results. From July 79 to January 80 21 patients with advanced squamous-cell carcinoma at the head and neck region were treated in a controlled pilot study with Cisplatinum/Bleomycin or Methotrexate/vindesine. 6 patients were primarily treated with chemotherapy, all other secondary progressive disease after surgical and x-ray procedure. Without respect to the generally cell tolerated therapy modality on overall remission induction rate of 50 and 70% was observed. In a subsequent randomized controlled multicentric study both regimes will be compared concerning remission, survival and toxicity.</AbstractText>
        </Abstract>
